# tiktoken's vocabulary cache files (docs/adr/ADR-003-token-estimation-strategy.md
# Addendum) are raw binary data named by a content hash - any line-ending
# normalization on checkout would silently corrupt them and break offline token
# estimation in a very confusing way (checksum mismatch, falls back to a network
# fetch that then fails). Git's own binary-detection heuristic already treats them
# as binary today, but this makes it explicit and permanent regardless of that
# heuristic or anyone's local core.autocrlf setting.
src/AI.Document.Converter.Python/tiktoken_cache/* binary

# Generated sample fixtures (docs/16-TEST-STRATEGY.md Section 3) - same reasoning,
# made explicit rather than relying on Git's heuristic.
samples/*.docx binary
samples/*.xlsx binary
samples/*.pptx binary
samples/*.pdf binary
